    {
      "id": "6787cd99-e5b3-41d8-ad48-6727b8928628",
      "farmer_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "role": "assistant",
      "message": "Hello Ramesh Gowda! Regarding your Rice (Day 35, Seedling Establishment & Early Vegetative):\n\n• Field Focus: Maintain optimal moisture in the root zone. Avoid standing water during non-critical phases.\n• Irrigation & Nutrition: Allow periodic aeration (alternate wetting and drying) to stimulate deep root growth.. Apply scheduled top dressing only when soil is moist and weather is clear.\n• Weather Impact: High rain probability detected in the next 24-48 hours. Consider postponing pesticide/foliar spraying and ensure field drainage channels are clear.\n• Safety Advisory: For any chemical spray, strictly adhere to label instructions and consult your nearest Krishi Vigyan Kendra (KVK) or call the Kisan Call Center (1800-180-1551).\n\nSource: ICAR Agronomic Package of Practices (Verified Fallback)",
      "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:14:28.752Z"
    },
